{%- comment -%} The estate's story in three short parts, each beside a photo (adapted from about-story-picture). {%- endcomment -%}
<section class="bg-base-100 text-base-content">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-[80rem] space-y-20 px-5 py-20 md:px-8 md:py-28">
    <div class="grid items-center gap-10 lg:grid-cols-12" data-reveal>
      <img src="/media/story-cherries.jpg" class="aspect-[4/3] w-full rounded-box object-cover lg:col-span-5">
      <div class="lg:col-span-6 lg:col-start-7">
        <p class="eyebrow text-base-content/75">1931 to 1997</p>
        <h2 class="mt-4 text-[clamp(2rem,2.6vw+1rem,3.25rem)]">The cherry hill</h2>
        <p class="body-copy mt-5 max-w-[56ch]">Hanne's grandfather planted tart cherries on the south face of the hill in 1931, half a mile from the lake, whose water keeps the late spring frosts off the blossom. For sixty-seven years the Vossbergs shook cherries into canvas every July.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="grid items-center gap-10 lg:grid-cols-12" data-reveal>
      <img src="/media/story-budbreak.jpg" class="aspect-[4/3] w-full rounded-box object-cover lg:col-span-5 lg:col-start-8 lg:row-start-1">
      <div class="lg:col-span-6 lg:col-start-1 lg:row-start-1">
        <p class="eyebrow text-base-content/75">1998</p>
        <h2 class="mt-4 text-[clamp(2rem,2.6vw+1rem,3.25rem)]">Four acres of Riesling</h2>
        <p class="body-copy mt-5 max-w-[56ch]">After the glut of 1997 left the fruit unpicked, Hanne pulled the top orchard and planted Riesling on the gravel where the trees had struggled most. The vines liked what the cherries didn't; the rest of the hill followed, block by block.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="grid items-center gap-10 lg:grid-cols-12" data-reveal>
      <img src="/media/barn-snow.jpg" class="aspect-[4/3] w-full rounded-box object-cover lg:col-span-5">
      <div class="lg:col-span-6 lg:col-start-7">
        <p class="eyebrow text-base-content/75">Since 1911</p>
        <h2 class="mt-4 text-[clamp(2rem,2.6vw+1rem,3.25rem)]">The barn</h2>
        <p class="body-copy mt-5 max-w-[56ch]">The fieldstone dairy barn at the top of the hill holds the bar, made from the boards of the last cherry trees, a stove for the winter and the cask cellar underneath. Its porch looks south over the rows to the lake.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
